<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e4149ada-4a67-54cf-8c76-8cfb9546d230" activityNameId="33b083e8-1e84-5c3e-8efa-82bfc3b08a68" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Sugar, from sugar beet, at sugar refinery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Sugar, from sugar beet, at sugar refinery
Inventory refers to the production of 1 kg sugar, respectively 1 kg of molasses (72% dry matter) and 1 kg of pulps (25.6% dry matter). The multioutput-process 'sugar beet, in sugar refinery' delivers the co-products 'sugar, from sugar beet, at sugar refinery' and 'molasses, from sugar beet, at sugar refinery' and 'pulps, from sugar beet, at sugar refinery. Economic allocation with allocation factor for common stages of 91.7% to sugar, 4.5% to molasses and 3.8% to pulps. Allocation is done according to carbon balance for CO2 emissions.;
UUID: 7a87d893-3c50-336d-98d6-b882bffcddbb
This dataset includes the transport of sugar beets to the sugar refinery, and the processing of sugar beets to sugar, molasses (72% dry matter) and pulps (25.6% dry matter). System boundary is at the sugar refinery. Treatment of waste effluents is included. Packaging of the sugar is not included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Sweet juice is extracted from the sugar beets by diffusion. The juice is then purified and crystallized to sugar. Molasses come as a by-product of the crystallization process.
Time period: Data from 1998 to 2005, typical technology for the production of sugar from sugar beet
Production volume: Production of sugar was 250 kt in Switzerland in 2004
Sampling: Data is from sugar producer in CH, industrial data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7a87d893-3c50-336d-98d6-b882bffcddbb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
